    "input": "search_document: I cannot access your specific order details (Order #10245) to verify the exact timestamp of your purchase or the specific items included in your shipment. Therefore, I cannot confirm if you are currently within the 24-hour window or explain the specific breakdown of your $120.00 charge without that data.\n\nHowever, based on the handbook excerpts provided, here is the policy information regarding your questions:\n\n**1. Address Change Cost and Timing**\n*   **Within 24 hours:** You may change your shipping address within 24 hours of placing your order at no additional cost [shipping:5].\n*   **After 24 hours:** After 24 hours, a $10.00 administrative fee applies to address changes [shipping:5].\n*   **System Lock:** You may modify your order details, including the shipping address, up to 24 hours after placing the order. After this 24-hour window, the order is locked in our system and cannot be edited manually [order_changes:1]. If you need to change the address after this period, you must cancel the order and place a new one, subject to our cancellation policy [order_changes:1].\n*   **Post-Dispatch:** Once the tracking number has been generated and the package has left our warehouse, address changes are no longer possible [shipping:5].\n\n**2. Shipping Cost Discrepancy ($85.00 vs. $120.00)**\n*   **Base Freight Cost:** The base freight cost is $85.00 for a single large item [shipping:4].\n*   **Additional Items:** Additional large items incur a surcharge of $40.00 each [shipping:4].\n*   **Possible Explanation:** If your order included more than one large item (e.g., the bike plus another bulky camping gear item), the cost would be $85.00 + $40.00 = $125.00. If you were charged exactly $120.00, it is possible that the order included one large item and other non-freight items, or there was a specific combination of fees not detailed in the \"single large item\" base rate. However, the handbook explicitly states that additional large items cost $40.00 each [shipping:4]. It is also possible that the $120.00 charge includes other fees not listed in the provided excerpts, or that the \"single large item\" definition was applied differently to your specific configuration.\n\n**Recommendation:**\nSince I cannot verify your specific order status or the exact composition of your shipment to explain the $120.00 charge or confirm if the 24-hour window has passed, I must escalate this ticket to a human agent. They can access Order #10245 to check the timestamp, verify if the address can still be changed, and provide a detailed breakdown of the shipping charges.\n\nPlease allow me to escalate this to a human agent for immediate assistance with your order.",
